WEBVTT

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.700
Thanks.

00:00:30.310 --> 00:00:31.280
What's up?

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:33.980
The practice session hasn't started yet...

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:36.610
Where is that idiotic manager?

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.650
The coach's missing too...

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.540
Is it really okay, manager...

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:49.850
...for you not to be there?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:55.310
Life's much easier for those who get ordered around.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.400
They'll get satisfied as long as it remains easy for them.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:40.380
He left the pitch just like that.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:43.410
How irresponsible can he be?

00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:47.060
What the hell's with self-practice? Don't screw with me!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:49.280
The atmosphere's just unpleasant.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.580
It's bad. Someone do something please!

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.600
I guess Dori, the oldest among us, will be...

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.250
Keepers, shall we do some practice?

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.270
Eh? Only goalkeeping?!

00:03:04.270 --> 00:03:06.510
Keepers have a different training menu, right?

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:08.990
T-That's just...

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.260
I guess there's no other choice.

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:19.080
I will be the temporary captain!

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:24.810
For starters, practice your passing in groups of three for warm-up!

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.950
Who's taking charge? Check it out.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.020
O-Okay. Kuroda...

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.530
Sugie too, perhaps.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:39.140
Those guys huh?

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.090
What's the meaning of doing this, manager?

00:03:43.370 --> 00:03:44.680
To observe them...

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.970
Just to see what will happen to them now that I've removed Murakoshi.

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.300
Whether they can pull it through or not...

00:03:54.020 --> 00:03:55.570
...depends on them now.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:03.790
Nice interception!

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:05.850
Hey that's cheating, Kuroda!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.040
Oh, shut up.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.400
Hey Kuro!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:10.310
What?

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.240
He's coming from the side! Stop him!

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:18.160
Nice!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:20.930
You're fast, just as I thought.

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:21.970
N-Not really.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.980
Hey, you guys!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:26.480
What are you guys doing?

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.270
Oh, it has started.

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:32.300
Let's go, Macchan!

00:04:34.520 --> 00:04:37.520
I thought I said to practice passing in groups of three.

00:04:37.850 --> 00:04:40.390
Why are you guys playing by yourselves?

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.170
Why can't we?

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:44.480
It's self-practice, anyway.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.650
Akasaki, you brat...

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:49.840
You have a problem with me?

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.320
I won't say that our usual training menu is bad.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.600
But I want to do something more practical.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.870
Isn't this what the manager wanted us to do?

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:05.060
That won't work.

00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.370
Why is that?

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:09.780
Listen up, you brat!

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:14.740
Whether we win or not in the opening matches of the season depends on us.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.020
That's why teamwork is very important.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:20.610
Our battle has already started long ago.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:24.310
Isn't that what Murakoshi says every year?

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:32.020
You're not allowed to do things on your own! Everyone else, do the same thing too!

00:05:32.530 --> 00:05:34.360
This is how teamwork is developed!

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:38.080
Can we win with that?

00:05:39.460 --> 00:05:43.790
We've been doing that all the while, but we haven't won anything yet, have we?

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.230
Akasaki, you...

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:49.950
I'll get you for that!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.340
Cut it out, Kuroda!

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:57.000
You're rejecting what Koshi's been doing for the team!

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:58.760
Enough, Kuroda.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:00.950
Koshi...?

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:03.120
Are we done?

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:05.940
Let's continue!

00:06:08.340 --> 00:06:11.020
Those guys are unforgivable.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:13.020
Don't think I'll let it go just like that!

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.150
Even though you were saying about teamwork just now...

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.000
Tsubaki.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.530
That includes you too.

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:28.170
This looks bad, manager. The team will be torn apart if this goes on!

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:32.510
What are you being happy about?!

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:37.110
Shall we go there now?

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:40.230
You finally feel like doing that?

00:06:40.970 --> 00:06:43.830
No, I just thought of something to heat it up even more...

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:47.950
Chase, chase it!

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:49.240
Cross it, Kurosa!

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:57.390
Manager?

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.040
Where are you going?

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:03.610
The ball!

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:06.310
I'm free here!

00:07:06.310 --> 00:07:07.190
Pass it!

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:10.190
Sorry about that.

00:07:12.390 --> 00:07:14.010
What are you doing, manager?

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:19.040
Manager, I'm done collecting the balls!

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:23.620
Okay, let's go!

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.360
Hold up, what are you planning to do?

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:35.290
There's one here too...

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.450
We're soccer players.

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.620
We can't practice without balls.

00:07:42.590 --> 00:07:43.260
Oh really.

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.230
I'll give you one then.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:48.200
W-What?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:52.890
Use this ball together with everyone, you hear me?

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:58.530
What's wrong? Hurry up before your body cools down!

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.720
That's just nice, isn't it?

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.640
Shall we have another match again?

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:11.350
I'm fine with using the same team. I'm sure you guys won't lose again, right?

00:08:12.070 --> 00:08:13.380
If you're fine with it, that is.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:17.240
You're getting cocky just because you won once, Akasaki.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.850
There's a limit to it, brat.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:22.830
We're going to practice passing with everyone.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:24.710
Get out if you're not going to do it.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.820
You're chickening out?

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:35.700
What's important are our basics. What can you do if you don't even believe in yourself?

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:39.030
We can't win if we don't change!

00:08:39.470 --> 00:08:40.990
I've had enough of you!

00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:43.770
Cut it out, Kuroda!

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:45.110
Please stop it!

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:46.490
Akasaki, you brat!

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:51.340
We're weak in both of them. Shouldn't we practice more instead?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:56.570
Then shouldn't we be focusing more on our specialties?

00:08:56.730 --> 00:09:00.010
You're one to say. Are you aiming to be a regular?

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.120
What's with that?!

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.200
I'll be practicing my dribbles...

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.870
I understand the situation now.

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.550
Huh, what?

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:20.130
Is this a part of your plan too, manager?

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:24.180
N-No, I missed the right timing to stop them.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.930
Stop it, all of you!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:30.280
They're scuffling out there! It'll get into the papers! Get a photo of it!

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:35.220
My, isn't it rather lively?

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:36.880
This year's camp...

00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:40.280
Who do you think you are, brat?!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.980
You're one to talk, you wimp!

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.030
You guys, cut it out now!

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:49.380
My, isn't it cold out here?

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:53.750
Why are you guys training in such a cold place?

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.130
Won't you get a cold?

00:09:57.240 --> 00:10:00.260
Where have you been all this time, Prince?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.440
Don't get mad.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:10.060
Captain, I thought we're gonna practice in the South so I was waiting for you guys at Okinawa.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.310
So, you're the new manager?

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:19.390
Yes.

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:21.640
You're young. How old are you?

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:22.680
Thirty-five.

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:26.630
No way! You're still in good shape to play, right?

00:10:27.070 --> 00:10:30.900
But you've got some aura about you that I am unable to guess.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.080
Luigi Yoshida. My nick's Gino.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.130
But people go around calling me the Prince.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:40.530
And he was the one making us do so...

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:44.670
Tatsumi Takeshi. My nick's Tatsu.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.870
You're cool.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:50.190
So, what are you guys doing?

00:10:50.840 --> 00:10:56.710
Well, we're doing self-practice just as the manager said, but things haven't been going so well.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.640
That sounds fun!

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:04.860
Well, I'll be joining the practice tomorrow.

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:09.280
I'm going rest for today. Where is the hotel?

00:11:10.150 --> 00:11:13.550
Show me the way. My room is there, right?

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:18.400
I'm sorry about that, manager. That was one of the regulars...

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.660
I know. I've looked through the list, afterall.

00:11:23.190 --> 00:11:28.060
Still, it's intriguing. Everyone stopped what they were doing the moment he came in.

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:44.300
What are you going to do about the starting line-up?

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:47.310
The league season's beginning soon!

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:55.530
Also, we have a pre-season match against the champs, Tokyo Victory, next week!

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.050
What are you getting impatient over, Gotou?

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:02.950
If the house is not built well, it'll get blown away by the wolf!

00:12:03.480 --> 00:12:05.030
What are you talking about?

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.590
The three little pigs.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:13.020
If we're going to build a house, we might as well build a strong one.

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:17.090
Also, the starting players are pretty much decided already.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.930
It's open! Let's go!

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:25.270
Akasaki, get into the center!

00:12:29.060 --> 00:12:29.610
Are you alright?

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:31.620
Akasaki?

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:35.410
That hurts! What the hell's that for?!

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.480
Your're just physically weak.

00:12:40.010 --> 00:12:41.970
Do you even bother about the consequences?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.980
Where are your manners?!

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.340
Cut it out, you guys.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:51.030
It's Tsubaki's turn.

00:12:51.840 --> 00:12:54.150
He did rather well in the previous match.

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:57.610
The coaches at the farm clubs were full of praise for him.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:04.030
Yeah, he was one of the hopefuls among the youngsters in the previous match.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:08.260
We put our hopes on him and gave him a good number.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.520
But for this camp...

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.250
...he has not been performing up to standard.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.050
Are you sleeping, Tsubaki? Go for ten rounds, now!

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:28.640
Yes!

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.390
What about him, Macchan?

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.580
Oh, Prince?

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:43.030
He's not at his best yet, so I told him to go do some self-practice.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.080
Yoshida!

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:53.940
Oh please, manager.

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:57.800
Call me Gino or the Prince.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.950
I don't want to, Yoshida.

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.370
I haven't seen you play yet.

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:07.020
I'll continue calling you Yoshida if you don't show me your skills.

00:14:07.590 --> 00:14:11.480
I'll take your number ten away. Is that alright with you, Yoshida?

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.270
Fine, I get it.

00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:20.370
I'm still not in top form yet, but I'll play with the guys over there.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:24.970
There's a bunch of good defenders over there now.

00:14:26.660 --> 00:14:31.110
As for my side, I'll pick that guy,

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.560
and the guy over there.

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.050
I'm Tsubaki Daisuke.

00:14:41.970 --> 00:14:43.750
Please take good care of me!

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:46.620
Baki, eh?

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:51.240
Ok then, I'll tell you your roles.

00:14:55.840 --> 00:14:59.600
I'll have you support me, as the dogs of the prince.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.650
What? Are they doing some sort of mini-game?

00:15:03.230 --> 00:15:06.390
Murakoshi's team versus the Prince and the youngsters...

00:15:07.530 --> 00:15:09.610
Crush them.

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:12.980
And show them your pride as the captain!

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:14.980
Mr ETU.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:20.600
What the hell's he thinking, that Gino? And being late for the practice too...

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.400
Anyway, just don't leave any holes for them to attack.

00:15:24.720 --> 00:15:26.080
Dori, I'll leave the commanding to you.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:27.280
Got it!

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:29.080
Don't let your guard down.

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:30.330
Yes, Koshi!

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:35.830
Why did the Prince choose Akasaki and Tsubaki?

00:15:36.150 --> 00:15:38.280
He could have chosen the others too...

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.630
He can boast around if he wins.

00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:42.850
Even if he loses, he can make excuses about it.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.190
Isn't that what he's planning for?

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.410
Run, Tsubaki, run!

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.780
You have nothing but speed.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:04.430
Don't underestimate us regular players!

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:08.040
What's wrong, Gino?

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:08.980
Prince!

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:15.820
What's with Tsubaki, running around aimlessly?

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.910
Listen, I'll have you guys be my dogs.

00:16:24.090 --> 00:16:25.060
What?!

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:30.630
Zaki will be the watch dog. You'll help me out when I'm in a pinch.

00:16:31.860 --> 00:16:34.190
And Baki, you'll be the stupid hunting dog.

00:16:34.810 --> 00:16:38.700
Just run around the pitch, as if you're chasing a hare.

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.650
Prince, I'm passing it back to you!

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:44.630
Zaki, your passing is weak!

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:53.620
He got it!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.330
Even though it seemed like a weak pass too.

00:16:57.830 --> 00:17:00.640
That's enough, Baki. Pass it back!

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.720
Do a follow up, Zaki.

00:17:09.720 --> 00:17:10.510
Tsubaki!

00:17:11.160 --> 00:17:15.820
They're quite a good combination, the Prince and Tsubaki.

00:17:16.590 --> 00:17:19.170
He's just running around aimlessly.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:22.940
The one who's doing those precise passes,

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:25.460
...while scanning the pitch for any holes,

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:27.790
...is that Italian brat, isn't it?

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:31.050
In the end, he's just showing off, eh.

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:37.730
It's amazing, that Prince! He's passing it to me precisely no matter where I am!

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:39.810
Don't screw with me!

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.420
That was close.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:50.920
Seeing how you guys are running around, it just makes it more fun to pass the ball around!

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.980
It's just speed and stamina, right?

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:58.240
If that is all it takes, then anyone would be able to play soccer.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.510
What's wrong, Koshi?

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:05.150
You're lacking your usual sharpness.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.080
A perfect goal!

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:21.650
Did you see that, Tatsumi?

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:25.020
Thanks for the hard work, guys! It was a good game.

00:18:27.720 --> 00:18:30.290
Never mind the Prince...

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.670
Murakoshi lost to the youngsters again!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:44.450
Impending breakdown due to internal conflict at ETU...

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:49.330
Will they be able to play the pre-season match?

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.740
"Bite your enemies while they are complacent."

00:18:53.010 --> 00:18:55.350
Tatsumi is that kind of guy.

00:18:56.100 --> 00:18:58.450
But we, the Tokyo Victory...

00:18:59.380 --> 00:19:02.820
...go all out to crush our opponents, no matter who they are.

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:22.040
What is this?

00:19:22.670 --> 00:19:26.800
This is our home ground, yet it's filled with Tokyo Victory's supporters!

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:30.710
Dad!

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:35.030
You really came! This is the first time I see you in that!

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:37.820
It's been quite a while...

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.340
But I suddenly feel like cheering for them as loud as I can!

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:43.270
You could have done that on some other day...

00:19:43.880 --> 00:19:44.570
What?

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:48.980
Their opponent is Tokyo Victory, the league champion for two consecutive years!

00:19:49.120 --> 00:19:51.780
There's even national players such as Mochida playing for them!

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:53.070
There's no way we can win!

00:19:53.390 --> 00:19:55.870
We're coming just because we're the students of the academy.

00:19:56.140 --> 00:19:57.990
You don't know anything at all eh, Kouta?

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.740
The new manager that you saw...

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:07.630
...is the kind of guy who goes wild the stronger his opponents are!

00:20:11.050 --> 00:20:12.960
Eh, no way.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.440
Stop fooling around!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:16.480
Kuro...

00:20:16.750 --> 00:20:18.480
Is that all there is to our strategy?

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:21.740
Also, we didn't practice much on our tactical plays.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.260
I'm fine as long as I can play.

00:20:25.280 --> 00:20:27.450
I'll do it! I'll definitely do it!

00:20:28.810 --> 00:20:32.370
Geez, you guys are really all split up, eh?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:37.520
Who's fault do you think it is?! You're the one who made this mess!

00:20:38.010 --> 00:20:40.480
Messing with all of us-

00:20:40.480 --> 00:20:41.340
Kuro!

00:20:41.640 --> 00:20:44.870
Don't think it'll all end up just as you planned it!

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:49.240
W-What is it?

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.320
I've never once thought about it in that way.

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:51.890
What?

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:57.300
Where's the fun in it if everything is going just as planned?

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.700
What's fun for me...

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.810
...is when something even greater than what I expect happens!

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:08.110
For example, the scrimmage game.

00:21:09.180 --> 00:21:11.490
The youngsters played a better game than I had expected.

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:16.220
During the camp, you guys came out with more methods to win than me.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:21.700
Both are just a little greater than what I thought.

00:21:25.460 --> 00:21:28.860
For this match, I'm guessing that we have a fifty-fifty chance of winning.

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:33.670
If you follow my strategy, I can ensure that it'll end up with a draw, at the very least.

00:21:34.780 --> 00:21:40.020
Whether you guys win or not depends on whether you can surpass your limits.

00:21:42.280 --> 00:21:43.860
So, what are you guys going to do?

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:46.670
Now's the time to decide if you're going to bet it all.

00:21:57.260 --> 00:21:59.570
Hey! The one with the captain armband is-

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:03.490
I don't like this.

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:07.980
I feel like a hoodlum, wearing this armband.

00:22:13.010 --> 00:22:16.690
Pleased to meet you, manager.

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:21.860
You're dandy as usual, Mr Hiraizumi.

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:27.040
I've heard about your achievements in England.

00:22:27.960 --> 00:22:34.990
Even though this is just a pre-season match, I'll be going all out against your team.

00:22:37.020 --> 00:22:38.450
Really, there's no need for that...

00:22:40.160 --> 00:22:43.370
Gino's the captain?

00:22:44.090 --> 00:22:46.470
And No.7 is a rookie...

00:22:47.140 --> 00:22:48.290
Interesting...

00:22:49.190 --> 00:22:50.400
That Tatsumi.

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:18.930
Keep that thirst to win.

00:24:20.570 --> 00:24:22.560
Never mind Akasaki and Sera.

00:24:22.770 --> 00:24:25.200
I think it's a little too early for Tsubaki.

00:24:25.990 --> 00:24:28.390
I...want to change!
